      "dom_id": "question-39995",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "What is the sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series $2+18+162+⋯?$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we determine the common ratio $r$ for this geometric series:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{18}{2} \\\\  & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series can be determined by the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{{a}_{1}(1-{r}^{N})}{1-r}.\n$$\n\nIn this case ${a}_{1}=2$ and $r=9.$ Substituting these values into the formula for ${S}_{N}$ gives the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{{a}_{1}(1-{r}^{N})}{1-r} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(1-{9}^{N})}{1-9} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(1-{9}^{N})}{(-8)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}(1-{9}^{N}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}({9}^{N}-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
